That's an excellent result. You used numbers which is very powerful.

1043
00:52:37,700 --> 00:52:40,580
Yes, numbers make the impact clear.

1044
00:52:40,580 --> 00:52:42,900
And finally, what did you learn?

1045
00:52:42,900 --> 00:52:48,260
I learned that clear communication between teams is essential for project success,

1046
00:52:48,260 --> 00:52:53,220
and that small design changes can have a big impact on user experience.

1047
00:52:53,220 --> 00:52:55,220
That is a strong conclusion.

1048
00:52:55,220 --> 00:52:55,940
Thank you.

1049
00:52:55,940 --> 00:52:58,980
Now let's talk about something very important.

1050
00:52:58,980 --> 00:53:01,780
Time management during your explanation.

1051
00:53:01,780 --> 00:53:06,660
Yes, because explaining a project for 30 minutes requires balance.

1052
00:53:06,660 --> 00:53:12,020
You don't want to spend 25 minutes on the beginning and only 5 minutes on results.

1053
00:53:12,020 --> 00:53:15,220
Exactly. You should divide your time carefully.

1054
00:53:15,220 --> 00:53:19,460
For example, you can spend a few minutes on the introduction and goal.

1055
00:53:19,460 --> 00:53:22,820
Then more time on the process and your role.

1056
00:53:22,820 --> 00:53:26,340
And also enough time on challenges and results.

1057
00:53:26,340 --> 00:53:30,180
Yes, because those parts show your problem-solving skills.

1058
00:53:30,180 --> 00:53:33,700
Another important tip is to use simple language.

1059
00:53:33,700 --> 00:53:35,940
Yes, especially in interviews.

1060
00:53:35,940 --> 00:53:38,820
clarity is more important than complexity.

1061
00:53:38,820 --> 00:53:44,900
For example, instead of using very technical words, explain ideas in a simple way.

1062
00:53:44,900 --> 00:53:49,220
Imagine you are explaining your project to someone outside your field.

1063
00:53:49,220 --> 00:53:52,500
That will make your explanation easier to understand.

1064
00:53:52,500 --> 00:53:55,060
And interviewers will appreciate that.

1065
00:53:55,060 --> 00:53:57,140
Let's talk about confidence.

1066
00:53:57,140 --> 00:54:01,300
Yes, many people feel nervous when speaking for a long time.

1067
00:54:01,300 --> 00:54:02,500
What can they do?

1068
00:54:02,500 --> 00:54:04,660
Practice is the best solution.

1069
00:54:04,660 --> 00:54:07,380
practice explaining your project out loud.

1070
00:54:07,380 --> 00:54:09,140
That's very important.

1071
00:54:09,140 --> 00:54:12,820
You can even record yourself and listen to your explanation.

1072
00:54:12,820 --> 00:54:15,700
That helps you improve structure and clarity.

1073
00:54:15,700 --> 00:54:18,660
Also, try to use natural transitions,

1074
00:54:18,660 --> 00:54:22,260
like first, then, after that, and finally.

1075
00:54:22,260 --> 00:54:24,660
Those words help guide the listener.

1076
00:54:24,660 --> 00:54:28,180
Yes, they make your explanation feel organized.

1077
00:54:28,180 --> 00:54:32,180
Let's give one final full example, combining everything.

1078
00:54:32,180 --> 00:54:33,140
Great idea!

1079
00:54:33,140 --> 00:54:34,100
Go ahead.

1080
00:54:34,100 --> 00:54:40,180
One project I worked on recently was improving internal communication within my company.

1081
00:54:40,180 --> 00:54:45,980
The goal was to reduce misunderstandings between departments and improve efficiency.

1082
00:54:45,980 --> 00:54:50,580
My role was to analyze communication problems and propose solutions.

1083
00:54:50,580 --> 00:54:51,820
Good start!

1084
00:54:51,820 --> 00:54:56,780
We began by collecting feedback from employees through surveys and interviews.

1085
00:54:56,780 --> 00:55:02,100
We discovered that many issues were caused by unclear instructions and lack of regular

1086
00:55:02,100 --> 00:55:03,100
updates.

1087
00:55:03,100 --> 00:55:09,740
very clear. Based on this, we introduced weekly team meetings and a shared online platform for updates.

1088
00:55:10,300 --> 00:55:14,780
One challenge was that some employees were not comfortable with new tools,

1089
00:55:14,780 --> 00:55:19,500
so we provided simple training sessions. Good problem-solving example.

1090
00:55:19,500 --> 00:55:25,180
After implementation, communication improved significantly and project delays decreased

1091
00:55:25,180 --> 00:55:32,220
by 20%. I learned that simple communication tools can make a big difference when used consistently.

1092
00:55:32,220 --> 00:55:34,380
That's an excellent explanation.

1093
00:55:34,380 --> 00:55:35,180
Thank you!

1094
00:55:35,180 --> 00:55:41,500
So, to summarize, explaining a project in 30 minutes is about telling a clear story.

1095
00:55:41,500 --> 00:55:45,900
Start simple, stay organized, and focus on what matters.

1096
00:55:45,900 --> 00:55:49,420
And always remember to explain your role clearly.

1097
00:55:49,420 --> 00:55:53,020
Yes, because that is what interviewers care about most.

1098
00:55:53,020 --> 00:55:55,580
Now we have a question for our listeners.

1099
00:55:55,580 --> 00:55:58,060
Yes, this is your practice task.

1100
00:55:58,060 --> 00:56:00,860
Can you describe a project you worked on?

1101
00:56:00,860 --> 00:56:05,660
Try to explain the goal, your role, the challenges, and the results.

1102
00:56:05,660 --> 00:56:07,820
You can practice speaking out loud.

1103
00:56:07,820 --> 00:56:10,140
Or write your answer and review it.

1104
00:56:10,140 --> 00:56:12,380
Thank you so much for listening today.

1105
00:56:12,380 --> 00:56:16,860
We hope this episode helps you feel more confident in your next interview.

1106
00:56:16,860 --> 00:56:19,420
Keep practicing your English every day.

1107
00:56:19,420 --> 00:56:23,340
And remember, clear communication is the key to success.

1108
00:56:23,340 --> 00:56:24,540
Goodbye, everyone.

1109
00:56:24,540 --> 00:56:25,420
See you next time.
